# Tests must pass before a pull request

Before `git push` or `gh pr create`, run the tests that cover every area this branch changes. Open the pull request only after those runs exit 0.

If any test fails, fix it and rerun until the same commands pass. Do not open the pull request with a failing or skipped required run.

## What to run

- Frontend changes (`public/`, `packages/`, `*.ts`, `*.tsx`): `yarn jest --watchAll=false` for the affected paths. Do not use `yarn test`; that script starts Jest in watch mode and does not exit.
- Backend changes (`pkg/`, `apps/`, `*.go`): `go test` for each affected package. Use `make test-go-unit` when the change spans many packages.
- Both frontend and backend: run both suites. A green run on one side does not cover the other.

## Before opening the pull request

State the exact commands you ran and that they passed. If you could not run a required suite, say so and do not open the pull request.
